00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:00.610
<b>I'll come straight to the point: what do you want to do now?</b>

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:05.240
<b>Can you come back tomorrow?</b>

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.790
<b>If I do that, you will have already decided your next step.</b>

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.250
<b>And it won't be what you want,</b>

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.790
<b>but something you settled on because you're out of time.</b>

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.630
<b>You know, you could still call it quits on the whole war right here.</b>

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:22.300
<b>Thenardier may be willing to negotiate,
depending on the conditions you offer him.</b>

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.350
<b>You <i>can</i> protect Alsace that way, you know?</b>

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:27.100
<b>What about your own goal?</b>

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:31.390
<b>I'll do what I can about that, of course.</b>

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.900
<b>Anyway...</b>

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:42.820
<b>Whatever we end up doing,
and however we decide to act,</b>

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:46.490
<b>I will fight my battles in a way I can take pride in.</b>

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:47.540
<b>That's all.</b>

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:51.660
<b>Take pride in them?</b>

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:53.290
<b>Yes.</b>

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.880
<b>I'll keep my pride as a warrior,</b>

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.750
<b>same as always.</b>

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.220
<b>See, I was a mercenary back in the day.</b>

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.890
<b>With no homeland to return to,</b>

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:09.860
<b>I just kept wandering the land,
looking for another fight.</b>

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.150
<b>Even my comrades-in-arms would die eventually,
leaving me with nothing to call my own.</b>

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.570
<b>That's why I have always held onto my pride. It lets me be who I am.</b>

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:22.820
<b>Pride...</b>

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:30.240
<b>If you've got your pride, then I've got my mettle!</b>

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:36.540
<b>I'm Tigrevurmud Vorn. I've learned from my father and many others to be brave!</b>

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.340
<b>Mettle...</b>

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.590
<b>Yeah, you're right.</b>

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:47.470
<b>That's how we define ourselves.</b>

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:55.750
<b>Titta.</b>

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:05.320
<b>Thank you. I know I must've worried you.</b>

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.240
<b>I'm sorry.</b>

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.330
<b>Count Tigre!</b>

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:29.390
<b>Once this war is over, we'll return to Alsace,</b>

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.140
<b>hold a funeral for Bertrand,
and spend the night remembering him.</b>

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:37.140
<b>Yes! We will!</b>

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:48.160
<b>Apparently Bertrand was concerned
that I would ignore events outside of Alsace.</b>

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:52.160
<b>But at the end he no longer had to worry.</b>

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.330
<b>I see.</b>

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:58.250
<b>Anyway, it's about time you finally realize
the other reason why I've been helping you.</b>

00:05:58.250 --> 00:05:58.920
<b>Huh?</b>

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.920
<b>I'm not here out of pure sentimentality—
there's a more practical reason too.</b>

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.170
<b>More practical?</b>

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:09.140
<b>Why did Muozinel attack Brune's south?</b>

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:11.510
<b>Why did they try to take control of a port town?</b>

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:15.890
<b>Well, it's a center of trade...</b>

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:16.810
<b>Hm?</b>

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:19.600
<b>Do you see where I'm going with this?</b>

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.900
<b>Fighting is not the only path forward...</b>

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.820
<b>Not the only... path?</b>

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.130
<b>The Vosges Mountains...</b>

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:49.180
<b>If we restore the highway
connecting Alsace and Leitmeritz,</b>

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.010
<b>then Leitmeritz would be...</b>

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:51.680
<b>That's right.</b>

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:58.930
<b>War is not just a way to obtain land and wealth.</b>

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:03.480
<b>It can be used to open roads
to new cultures and products,</b>

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:05.440
<b>enriching your territory in the process.</b>

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.440
<b>And Alsace...</b>

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:11.740
<b>...is guaranteed to change as well. 
For better or for worse.</b>

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.740
<b>However, it takes a competent leader,</b>

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:18.250
<b>governing with everything that's happening in mind, to make a difference.</b>

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.460
<b>"Everything that's happening", huh?</b>

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:27.340
<b>Hey, there...</b>

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.260
<b>How long have you been there?</b>

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:35.220
<b>Th-This Bruneman wasn't doing his work, so...</b>

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:39.390
<b>This Zhctedian was so fidgety,
I couldn't concentrate.</b>

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:43.350
<b>We've all been waiting for you.</b>

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.270
<b>There you have it.</b>

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:50.030
<b>Thanks, everyone.</b>

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.290
<b>Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Brune,</b>

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.670
<b>Pierre Badouin, at your service.</b>

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:09.630
<b>I'm relieved to find you
alive and well, Princess Regin.</b>

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.510
<b>I heard about everything
that happened from His Majesty.</b>

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.050
<b>I see.</b>

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.390
<b>It's a pleasure to make your acquaintance, Prime Minister.</b>

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:18.680
<b>Not quite.</b>

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:23.600
<b>I met you once before, when you
accompanied your father to the palace.</b>

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:27.190
<b>It has been too long, Sir Tigrevurmud.</b>

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.110
<b>Oh...</b>

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.070
<b>So, what brings you here, Badouin?</b>

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:34.030
<b>His Majesty, the king, is feeling better.</b>

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:39.080
<b>It appears he was being poisoned by Duke Ganelon.</b>

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:39.830
<b>What?!</b>

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:41.950
<b>Sir Tigrevurmud,</b>

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.620
<b>would you mind telling me your intentions?</b>

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:49.750
<b>What do you plan to do hereafter?</b>

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:54.430
<b>I will fight Duke Thenardier and strike him down.</b>

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.090
<b>And what are your plans for Brune?</b>

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.260
<b>Nothing.</b>

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:01.350
<b>Once I've made sure Alsace will stay safe,</b>

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.060
<b>I'll return to being a Zhctedian prisoner.</b>

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.560
<b>H-Hold on!</b>

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.150
<b>I'm sure we can put that in nicer words!</b>

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.270
<b>Very true.</b>

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:11.780
<b>If you'd prefer, I'm willing to welcome you as a guest of honor.</b>

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.190
<b>You shut up, pipsqueak!</b>

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:15.070
<b>No, <i>you</i> shut up!</b>

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:19.160
<b>Are you really doing this merely to protect Alsace?</b>

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.030
<b>I am.</b>

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.500
<b>Though there's one more thing I'd like to say.</b>

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:28.130
<b>If Alsace can't be kept safe within Brune,</b>

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:34.630
<b>I'd consider it becoming part of Zhcted.</b>

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:42.180
<b>Well then, Badouin, what would you suggest we do?</b>

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:49.150
<b>Take Her Highness with you and hurry to Nice.</b>

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:52.900
<b>His Majesty's life will probably not last much longer.</b>

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:02.910
<b>Duke Thenardier will most likely try
to keep us from entering the royal capital.</b>

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:10.330
<b>It's the final showdown.</b>

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:28.350
<b>The two armies clash in the wilds of Mereville.</b>

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.910
<b>You don't have to worry.</b>

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:50.620
<b>The chivalric orders cover the right flank,</b>

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.880
<b>while Rurick and the Zhctedian forces are holding the left flank.</b>

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:54.920
<b>And the center—</b>

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:59.260
<b>That's not what worries me.
Should I really be the supreme commander?</b>

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:01.140
<b>Sir Tigrevurmud ought to...</b>

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:05.010
<b>We are fighting this battle so <i>you</i>
can enter the capital, Your Highness.</b>

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.600
<b>Only you, Your Highness, are fit to take command.</b>

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:09.380
<b>I see.</b>

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:13.110
<b>We definitely have the upper hand.</b>

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:14.320
<b>However...</b>

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:17.070
<b>Thenardier's forces should not be so disorganized.</b>

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.610
<b>At first I worried it might be a trap,</b>

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:26.120
<b>but it appears Steed, who led
Thenardier's army, <i>did</i> die at the Holy Grotto.</b>

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:36.730
<b>Still, Duke Thenardier should be here and commanding them personally—</b>

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:37.920
<b>He isn't.</b>

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.420
<b>And we're about to see why.</b>

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:42.930
<b>You don't mean...!</b>

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:49.310
<b>So you've come.</b>

